<worksheet>
    <title> Session #11 (Section 4.6)</title>
    <p>
      Directions: Answer each of the following as best you can. Feel free to discuss your thoughts about the questions with some peers around you. 
      For additional practice problems and explanations, refer to the Math 142 textbook which is free and can be downloaded as a PDF 
      at <url href="https://oaktrust.library.tamu.edu/items/03980291-5e85-4d2e-a742-961ac49666aa"> Texas A&amp;M The OAKTrust Digital Repository </url>.
      <!--'&' and '<' are exceptional characters and are instead authored as &lt; and &amp;. See 4.1.4.2-->
    </p>
    <paragraphs>
        <title>Getting Warmed Up and In the Right Mindset....</title>

    <exercise>
        <statement>
            <p>Shade in the area between the curves <m>f(x)</m> and <m>g(x)</m> on the interval <m>[-2,4]</m>.</p>

            <image source="Graphics/session11_1.png">
                <shortdescription>Graph of the functions used in the problem.</shortdescription>
            </image>
        </statement>
    </exercise>

    <exercise>
        <statement>
            <p>Shade in the area between the curves <m>g(x)</m> and <m>h(x)</m> on the interval <m>[-2,7]</m>.</p>

            <image source="Graphics/session11_1.png">
                <shortdescription>Graph of the functions used in the problem.</shortdescription>
            </image>
        </statement>
    </exercise>

    <exercise xml:id="session11-warmup-3">
        <statement>
            <p>Shade in the area bounded by the curves <m>h(x)</m> and <m>g(x)</m>.</p>

            <image source="Graphics/session11_1.png">
                <shortdescription>Graph of the functions used in the problem.</shortdescription>
            </image>
        </statement>
    </exercise>

    <exercise xml:id="session11-warmup-4">
        <statement>
            <p>Shade in the area bounded by the curve <m>g(x)</m> and the <m>x</m>-axis.</p>

            <image source="Graphics/session11_1.png">
                <shortdescription>Graph of the functions used in the problem.</shortdescription>
            </image>
        </statement>
    </exercise>

    </paragraphs>

    <paragraphs>
        <title>Let us get our hands on!</title>


